;; hello_world_rustix module — the extern-deps rust sample for divifetch-zig.
;;
;; :language "rust" with a :deps :ext entry turns the build script over to
;; cargo: the generator writes the crate manifest right here (the lib is
;; module.rs, the spellings are the [dependencies], and the release profile
;; pins panic=abort), the build runs `cargo build --release`, and zig links
;; the staticlib archive beside its own sources.
;;
;; the :ext spellings carry the crate name, its version requirement, the
;; no-default-features toggle and a features=[...] list with no spaces —
;; "rustix 1.1.6 features=[system]". features come along exactly as
;; cargo would read them; a no_std crate adds no-default-features and
;; keeps the std spelling off its :deps.
;;
;; the archive embeds std and every crate it rolls up, so the link needs
;; libc (:std) and libunwind (the generator adds it for :ext modules);
;; :linker-flags still ride the final link.
(module
    :language "rust"
    :fn "hello_world_rustix_module_preset"
    :deps [:std :ext ["rustix 1.1.* features=[system]"]])
